[?2004l[?2004h> Path(OUT/'report.md').write_text('''# Top-associated diphoton BDT categorization
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Introduction
[?2004l[?2004h> Hadronic-only H→γγ top-associated categorization using ATLAS open data.
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Data and Monte Carlo Samples
[?2004l[?2004h> Only nominal ggH, VBF, WH, ZH, ggZH, ttH and tH MC and GamGam data were read; Sherpa/prompt continuum MC were excluded.
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Object Definition and Event Selection
[?2004l[?2004h> Two kinematic photons (pT>25 GeV, |η|<2.37) are required without photon tight-ID or isolation. Electrons/muons have pT>10 GeV; jets pT>25 GeV; b tags use quantile≥4. Hadronic is 0 leptons, ≥3 jets and ≥1 b tag.
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Overview of the Analysis Strategy
[?2004l[?2004h> A deterministic five-variable BDT uses ttH+tH as signal and ggH plus NTI sideband data as background.
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Signal and Control Regions
[?2004l[?2004h> TI means both photons tight-ID and tight-isolation; NTI is its complement. TI signal-window observed data are blinded.
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Cut Flow
[?2004l[?2004h> See `cutflow.json` and ![](plots/preselection_channels.png).
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Distributions in Signal and Control Regions
[?2004l[?2004h> ![](plots/preselection_mass.png) ![](plots/score_by_component_shape_bdt_v1.png)
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Categorization
[?2004l[?2004h> ![](categorization/plots/category_expected_yields_36fb_v1.png) ![](categorization/plots/category_mgg_control_shapes_36fb_v1.png)
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Systematic Uncertainties
[?2004l[?2004h> This starting point retains signed MC-weight bookkeeping; no nuisance systematic variations are fitted.
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Statistical Interpretation
[?2004l[?2004h> ROOT/PyROOT/RooFit workspace artifacts use the sideband-only, blinded Asimov strategy. Observed significance is blocked.
[?2004l[?2004h> ![](fit/FIT1/plots/sidebands_background_fit.png) ![](fit/FIT1/plots/asimov_sb_fit.png)
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Artifact Checklist
[?2004l[?2004h> Machine-readable selection, training, inference, categorization, histograms and workspace manifests are present.
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> Expected 36 fb⁻¹ category yields use physical MC normalization and scaled NTI proxy, never class-balanced BDT weights.
